<SddCritic keywords="critic, orchestrator, spec-review, task-review, blind-spot, multi-round, reconcile, surgical-edit, sdd-critic" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Autonomous critique loop for SDD artifacts (spec / task / batch). I am the ORCHESTRATOR: per round
    I dispatch one isolated critic-sensor, evaluate its findings against full project context, reconcile
    every introduced entity against the existing surface via `orient` (reuse > extend > justify >
    escalate), surgically edit the artifact, and re-dispatch if edits were applied (cap 5). Batch: the
    scope spec first, then tasks in DAG layers (parallel within a layer, sequential between). On CLEAN:
    delete the temporary `## Critic Rounds` scratch. I own the artifact: apply every `MECHANICAL` edit
    directly, then ONE round checkpoint batches whatever needs the operator — `GOAL` findings as
    questions, plus a confirm/correct block for any `CRITICAL` / `MAJOR` fix just applied
    (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). The sensor only reports; only the operator downgrades a `GOAL` tag.

    A separate door (`/sdd-critic`). Input — a spec / task / batch target. Output — the cleaned artifact
    + the final verdict.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-language"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-dialogue-style"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-owner"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-isolation-signal"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-critic-model-tier"}}

    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-reuse-first"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-surgical"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-default-accept"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-confusion-bug"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-finding-addressee"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-goal-owner-gate"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-severity"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-rejection-reason"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-re-dispatch"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-stop-no-edits"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-cap-5"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-scratch-log"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-task-parallel"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_ARTIFACT` | The target spec / task does not exist |
    | `H_PARENT_SPEC_MISSING` | A task's parent spec is missing — cannot critique a task without its spec |
    | `H_DISPATCH_FAILED` | The sensor subagent failed to dispatch twice — surface to the operator, do not loop silently |
    | `H_MAX_ROUNDS` | Cap of 5 rounds hit and still not CLEAN — escalate to the operator (`AX_CAP_5`) |
    | `H_GOAL_BLOCKED` | `GOAL` findings block the round and the operator is unavailable to answer — stop, report the pending question block |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_RESOLVE">
      <Goal>Resolve the target.</Goal>
      <Action>Spec / task / batch (spec + its tasks — critiqued in DAG layers, parallel within a layer, per `AX_TASK_PARALLEL`). Missing → `H_NO_ARTIFACT`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_DISPATCH">
      <Goal>Dispatch the isolated sensor.</Goal>
      <Action>One fresh subagent, on a worker-tier model — never stronger than the author's model (`AX_CRITIC_MODEL_TIER`): read `ai/directives/sdd-v2/critic-protocol.directive.xml` + the artifact + parent spec only (`AX_ISOLATION_SIGNAL`). Emit a round progress line (`ORCHESTRATOR_PROGRESS_FORMAT`).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_EVALUATE">
      <Goal>Weigh findings against full project context.</Goal>
      <Action>Split by addressee (`AX_FINDING_ADDRESSEE`): `MECHANICAL` — accept by default (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`); `GOAL` — queue for STEP_3B, keep the touched sections intact (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). The sensor's `GOAL` tag is a floor, not a ceiling: downgrading it to `MECHANICAL` is the operator's call alone (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`) — an orchestrator read that leans mechanical carries into STEP_3B as one more question, never a private reclassification. A rejection cites a specific file / section that resolves the concern (`AX_REJECTION_REASON`). Sensor confusion the full context resolves = an artifact bug — clarify by edit (`AX_CONFUSION_BUG`); confusion the project cannot answer = `GOAL`. Also carry each finding's severity (`AX_SEVERITY`) forward — STEP_3B gates on it.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_RECONCILE">
      <Goal>Reconcile every introduced entity. (mechanical → tool)</Goal>
      <Action>For each entity a finding would add, run `orient` to check the existing project surface: reuse > extend > justify > escalate (`AX_REUSE_FIRST`). Do not let the critique invent a duplicate of an existing entity.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_EDIT">
      <Goal>Apply the round's `MECHANICAL` edits.</Goal>
      <Action>Edit only what a finding requires (`AX_SURGICAL`); I apply the edits — the sensor never does (`AX_OWNER`). Apply every `MECHANICAL` finding directly, regardless of severity (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`) — a `CRITICAL` / `MAJOR` mechanical finding gets fixed now, confirmed with the operator next at STEP_3B, not gated before the fix. Leave `GOAL`-tagged sections untouched — their edit waits for the operator's answer at STEP_3B. Record each edit in the temporary `## Critic Rounds` scratch (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3B_ROUND_CHECKPOINT">
      <Goal>One batch Ask per round for every operator-owned item (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Build ONE `AskUserQuestion` batch (`QUESTION_FORMAT` batching rule — independent questions ride
        together) carrying, when present: (a) every `GOAL` finding from STEP_2 as its own question,
        including any orchestrator disagreement with a sensor's `GOAL` tag («critic tagged GOAL, I read
        this as mechanical because …») — the tag stands until this answer says otherwise; (b) IF this
        round carried any `CRITICAL` / `MAJOR` finding (mechanical or goal), one confirm block: «critic
        found N problems this round, fixed as follows: <one line per fix> — confirm, or correct?».
        Neither (a) nor (b) applies (the round was `MINOR` / `INFO` only, or carried zero findings) →
        skip the Ask, go straight to STEP_4 (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`). WAIT for the answer
        before touching any `GOAL`-tagged section. Apply `GOAL` edits exactly as answered, and any
        correction the operator makes to a confirmed fix, recording each in `## Critic Rounds`
        (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`). Operator unreachable while `GOAL` findings block → `H_GOAL_BLOCKED`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_DECIDE">
      <Goal>Loop or stop.</Goal>
      <Action>Edits applied this round (STEP_3 or STEP_3B) → re-dispatch (`AX_RE_DISPATCH` — mandatory, no self-made exception for a fix judged trivial). Zero edits → stop (`AX_STOP_NO_EDITS`). Cap 5 (`AX_CAP_5`) → `H_MAX_ROUNDS`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Finalize.</Goal>
      <Action>On CLEAN: delete the `## Critic Rounds` scratch; the artifact is clean with improvements integrated. Report the final verdict (CLEAN | NEEDS_WORK | CRITICAL) with a one-line-per-round summary of what changed — the reported verdict MUST be the literal verdict text of the LAST sensor dispatch actually run (`AX_RE_DISPATCH`), shown as a direct quote, never a paraphrase and never an earlier round's verdict presented as current. A structural problem the critique cannot resolve by a surgical edit → escalate to the operator, do not loop.</Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

